            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous bail-out treatment of vein graft rupture with a polytetrafluoroethylene-covered stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/17482941.2013.835829</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vessel perforation is an undesirable and life-threatening complication during vein graft angioplasty. We report on a case of vein graft rupture during angioplasty, which was successfully managed with deployment of a polytetrafluoroethylene-covered stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
